@startuml mea-nexaworks
title NexaWorks — Entity-Relationship Model (issue tracking)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
hide circle
skinparam nodesep 80
skinparam ranksep 70


class Product {
  + Id : INT <<PK>>
  {field} + Name : NVARCHAR(100) <<unique>>
}

class Version {
  + Id : INT <<PK>>
  + ProductId : INT <<FK>>
  {field} + Number : NVARCHAR(10)
  --
  unique (ProductId, Number)
}

class OperatingSystem {
  + Id : INT <<PK>>
  {field} + Name : NVARCHAR(50) <<unique>>
}

class VersionOperatingSystem {
  + Id : INT <<PK>>
  + VersionId : INT <<FK>>
  + OperatingSystemId : INT <<FK>>
  --
  unique (VersionId, OperatingSystemId)
}

class Ticket {
  + Id : INT <<PK>>
  + VersionOperatingSystemId : INT <<FK>>
  + StatusId : INT <<FK>>
  + CreatedAt : DATE
  + ResolvedAt : DATE [0..1]
  {field} + Problem : NVARCHAR(MAX)
  {field} + Resolution : NVARCHAR(MAX) [0..1]
}

class Status {
  + Id : INT <<PK>>
  {field} + Label : NVARCHAR(20) <<unique>>
}

Product "1" -- "1..*" Version : has
Version "1" -- "1..*" VersionOperatingSystem : runs on
VersionOperatingSystem "0..*" -right- "1" OperatingSystem : supports
VersionOperatingSystem "1" -- "0..*" Ticket : reported on
Status "1" -- "0..*" Ticket : qualifies

note bottom of VersionOperatingSystem
  Join table Version <-> OperatingSystem (many-to-many).
  One row = one supported combination.
  A ticket points to an existing Version + OS pair:
  a ticket on an unsupported combination is impossible
  (e.g. Trader en Herbe 1.0 on iOS).
end note

note bottom of Ticket
  Status "Resolved"    => ResolvedAt and Resolution are filled
  Status "In progress" => ResolvedAt and Resolution are NULL
  ResolvedAt >= CreatedAt
end note
@enduml
